# Capability Theory, the Adaptive Markets Hypothesis, and High Frequency Trading (PowerPoint Presentation)

**Authors:** Ben Van Vliet

## Abstract
This PowerPoint presentation reviews the capability theory of how HFT firms make allocation decisions under the adaptive markets hypothesis. It shows how capability theory is precisely consistent with both expected utility theory and theories in behavior finance. Capability defines the point at which these firms reach the satisficing solution. Thus, capability theory provides a quantitative representation of the AMH, and allows us to move back an forth between mainstream theory and practice.

